{"reference":"1 Chronicles 16","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":16,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Historical Context","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents the ark’s arrival as part of an ordered, continuing pattern of worship: David assigns priests and Levites to serve before it, while other priests maintain the regular offerings at the tabernacle. This follows the earlier failed procession, when the ark was to be carried according to the prescribed order.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 16:1-43"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_016_0f524031c14a82055c80c531"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}